-- Every rejection inside the turn calls `onError` with an `Error`: an existing `Error` is passed through unchanged, while every other value is wrapped with a readable `message` and the original value as its `cause`; the caller still receives the original rejection unchanged, and `afterSession` then runs ([validated by: wraps a string rejection for onError while preserving it for the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L278), [validated by: passes an Error rejection through to onError unchanged](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L309), [validated by: calls onError with an Error carrying the thrown string and runs afterSession while rethrowing](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L53), [validated by: calls onError with an Error carrying a readable message when the stream rejects with a plain object](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L64)).
